WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.233
Everything on the Schedule.

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:11.867
The Schedule board. Crews down the side, days across, two weeks at a time. Every sold piece of work gets its crew and its days here.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:18.300
Move through the weeks. The arrows go back or forward a week; Today comes back to this week.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:25.833
Board or month. Crews · 2 weeks is this board; Month shows the whole month. We'll look at Month at the end.

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:33.700
To schedule. Every sold piece of work without a crew and a start day waits here, approved change orders too.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:45.267
Waiting work. Job colour, work name, customer, job number, town, crew-hours and when it was sold. A red Permit hold tag: it can be booked but can't start yet.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:50.333
Schedule it from here. The calendar button opens the schedule form.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:52.867
Crew. Pick the crew.

00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:55.933
Start. The first day on site.

00:00:56.433 --> 00:01:04.833
Budgeted crew-hours. Days = these hours ÷ the crew's hours a day. A preview of the days shows under the form.

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:10.300
Days. Or type the number of days yourself (0 = from the hours).

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.933
Book it. Schedule books it and tells you if the crew goes over capacity on any day. The tour doesn't press it.

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:23.100
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:31.200
Or drag it. Drag a card onto a crew's start day and the form opens there. Or click the card to pick it, like this …

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:38.433
… then click the day. … then click the crew's start day on the board: the form opens with that crew and day.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:42.700
Put it back. Click the picked card again to let go of it.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:49.800
Appointments row. How many sales visits and tasks there are each day, and whose. Hover for the times.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.600
A crew. Crew colour, name, lead and how many crew-hours it can do in a day.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:08.667
Booked work. One colour per job, the same every day it runs (↳ = continues). Click it to open the job; drag it to another day or crew to move it. A multi-day job moves together.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:18.667
How full the day is. The line under a day is the crew's load against what it can do. Faded blocks are done; work that has started can't be dragged.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:27.867
Over capacity. A red outline: the crew is booked for more hours than it can do that day. Move something to another day or crew.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:39.967
What the colours mean. Bars: one colour per job, faded = done. Each crew's colour and hours a day, the red over-capacity outline, and the lock for a permit hold.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.133
Month view. Shows the whole month.

00:02:43.633 --> 00:02:51.200
The month. Here a colour is a crew (the key is above). Click a bar to open the job; drag it to another day to move it.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:56.700
Other months. The arrows go a month back or forward; This month comes back.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.567
Back to the board. Crews · 2 weeks goes back to the crew board.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:07.667
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
